        {
            "number": 2,
            "revision": "37895feb26dbfa3175bcc0e8ecb40be4766e0069",
            "parents": [
                "d7be68dd3068d9fd4a4bbe7c8958b9dd57270a3c"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/72/74672/2",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                "username": "mox669"
            },
            "createdOn": 1727205618,
            "author": {
                "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                "username": "mox669"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "this capability already exists, although today it only supports setting asset tag.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/master/src/fru_device.cpp#L788\n\nwe'd need to update to a settable fru policy (probably settable in an em config or meson option) to determine which fields a user is allowed to set."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "That makes sense, will have a look at that!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: \"feat:\" isn't really a tag we use in openbmc for commit messages."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this intended to be used on a user-facing API?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "Similar question -- is renaming things like 'BOARD_PRODUCT_NAME' something folks would actually want to do on a production system, or is this mostly for debug purposes?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "@Ed beyond exposing this functionality on dbus nothing is planned for now, unlike the ASSET_TAG update that we can do via redfish.\n \n@Christopher we mainly have pre-production scenarios in mind for this feature, however we know of a case of one of our customers that updates some properties in production aswell.\nI can only assume that updating 'BOARD_PRODUCT_NAME' might have a case be it pre-production or production, but updating 'BOARD_SERIAL_NUMBER' for example shouldn't be really in the discussion. I feel like especially updating custom fru fields is something people are looking for."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> but updating 'BOARD_SERIAL_NUMBER' for example shouldn't be really in the discussion\n\nNot positive what you meant by that.  Using this in API manufacturing time might actually desire programming the serial number."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Oh ok I see, thanks for the insight. I then would assume there is case to be made for every other property defined by the specification?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Correct."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Got it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> @Ed beyond exposing this functionality on dbus nothing is planned for now\n\n\"for now\" makes it sound like you have something in mind for the future?  BTW, there's already mechanisms for updating asset tag through Redfish, so if that's your intent, that's fine and expected.  We can add more supported fields as needed.\n\n> I feel like especially updating custom fru fields is something people are looking for.\n\nFWIW, this is exactly what the Intel \"Manufacturing mode\" interface is supposed to support.  Should we hook into that, and say \"if in manufacturing mode, allow updating any fru field, else only allow expected user-modifyable fields?\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "> \"for now\" makes it sound like you have something in mind for the future?\n\nPoorly phrased sorry, there are no further plans from my side. \n\n> [..] so if that's your intent, that's fine and expected. We can add more supported fields as needed.\n\nThe goal is to allow updating every property, defined and custom - for testing purposes. It is not deciding on a set of supported properties. \n\n> BTW, there's already mechanisms for updating asset tag through Redfish, so if that's your intent, that's fine and expected.\n\nUpdate via Redfish is out of scope for this patch. \n    \n> FWIW, this is exactly what the Intel \"Manufacturing mode\" interface is supposed to support.\n\nAre you referring to this: https://github.com/openbmc/intel-ipmi-oem/blob/4843746a466f09f4592752e666eb0d15cabf54ee/include/manufacturingcommands.hpp#L69C1-L71C1 ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "As Ed mentioned in the following commit, The new method needs to be on the object path of the FRU being updated."
                }
            ],
