            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Needs to be in entity-manager config, with already exists with type: eeprom, just needs to be read out by fru-device and have a new field added."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Currently testing this approach. This type is not explicitly defined, got it working with a eeprom.json subschema though. I am not sure what you had in mind proceeding from there. Is the idea to then read out the UpdatableProperties field from dbus inside fru_device? This seems easiest at least."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Naresh Solanki",
                        "email": "naresh.solanki@9elements.com",
                        "username": "nsolanki22"
                    },
                    "message": "@ed@tanous.net\nIs below snippet aligned with your suggestion?\n```\n  \"Type\": {\n    \"title\": \"Configuration Type\",\n    \"description\": \"The schema for the type property. The type property identifies the type of the configuration.  When exported, configurations will be instantiated as children of: /xyz/openbmc_project/configuration/<Type>\",\n    \"enum\": [\n      \"Board\",\n      \"Chassis\",\n      \"NVMe\",\n      \"PowerSupply\",\n      \"CPU\",\n      \"Cable\",\n      \"Eeprom\"\n    ]\n  },\n\n  \"UpdatableProperties\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"areas\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"chassis\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"board\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"product\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          }\n        },\n      }\n    },\n  }```\n\nPlease let me know if this needs further changes"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Need reconciled with the support that already exists for this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 72,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This data needs to be coming from entity-manager, not a fixed json file on disk.  Add it as a value under the Type: \"Eeprom\" exposes record, and have fru device read it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 72,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 718,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "?  Pretty sure we don't want to crash all of fru-device because of a bad config."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 718,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 724,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Need to return here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 724,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 743,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "No need to structure code with a validateJson then call at().\n\nJust use \n\ndata.find(\"areas\");\n\nand handle the case where the iterator is end.  As written this will generate an exception for a case that can never happen, which bloats binary sizes."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 743,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 748,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "get_if here and handle the error."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 748,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 749,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "It seems really odd that this is just a fixed table of string entries?  Presumably it needs to be per FRU, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 749,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 941,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This needs to be a SetProperty method, which already exists and has examples\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/48c21ce1a532ffedf205a942b398255a5755aa85/src/fru_device.cpp#L1208\n\n\nWe shouldn't be registering a new dbus method when there's already a mechanism registered to do this:\n\nregistration is here.\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/48c21ce1a532ffedf205a942b398255a5755aa85/src/fru_device.cpp#L854"
                },
                {
